00:15:10,340 --> 00:15:12,460
Okay, we got 45 minutes to hit the other 57.

256
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:15,400
I think we can do it.

257
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:31,220
Ah, bonjour, papa.

258
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:34,320
Jason, where have you been?

259
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:36,660
You said you'd be back at seven, and it's...

260
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:38,420
and it's, um, five till.

261
00:15:39,820 --> 00:15:41,220
Well, I thought you wanted me to get out.

262
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:43,420
Of course I said that.

263
00:15:43,620 --> 00:15:44,920
I didn't really think you'd go.

264
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:46,700
I just thought you'd stay.

265
00:15:46,700 --> 00:15:47,640
You thought what?

266
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:50,900
That you could leave me in this crummy room while you went out and had a wonderful

267
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:52,520
time in Paris, the city of lights?

268
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:54,660
Maggie. You said you wouldn't have fun.

269
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:57,960
You promised. I found Henri.

270
00:15:59,340 --> 00:16:03,120
What? Yes. Exactly where we left it 22 years ago.

271
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:06,160
I even ordered from the same menus printed on the wine bottle.

272
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:07,500
Oh, that figures.

273
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:08,840
That just figures.

274
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:14,640
You probably had a wonderful dinner and a wonderful champagne and witty conversation

275
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:15,660
with exotic women.

276
00:16:15,860 --> 00:16:17,800
Just probably. You remember Henri?

277
00:16:18,160 --> 00:16:19,540
Ah, Madame Sieber.

278
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:22,900
In 20 years, you only look lovely.

279
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:25,640
No, Henri, Henri.

280
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:27,640
Oh, my God.

281
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:35,460
Madam Sieber, in 20 years, you only look lovely.

282
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,760
May I serve you now?

283
00:16:46,260 --> 00:16:52,520
Oh, jeez. You are the sweetest, most thoughtful husband a woman could ever have.

284
00:16:52,540 --> 00:16:53,900
Yeah, I've been saying that for years.

285
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:04,600
Jason Seabert. Will you marry me?

286
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:07,480
I'm thinking about it.

287
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:14,520
Ooh. Whoa, Paris.

288
00:17:15,060 --> 00:17:17,800
Heh. Well, I think we finally got out of Spain.

289
00:17:18,920 --> 00:17:19,720
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

290
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:21,500
Easy, Maurice. We don't want to hit this thing.

291
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:24,560
I dreamed I'd see Paris like this.

292
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:25,620
Hey, the river's safe.

293
00:17:25,620 --> 00:17:27,320
In the Notre Dame Cathedral.

294
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:29,480
And that's the Louvre and the Arc de Triomphe.

295
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:32,900
Items 47, 48, and 49 on your itinerary, everyone.

296
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:49,660
Oh, could you put us down in that beautiful park?

297
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:54,040
Ooh, we. Okay, fine, because you put we down in that beautiful park.

298
00:17:54,040 --> 00:18:02,620
Same gets. Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

299
00:18:02,700 --> 00:18:03,720
Set her down easy, Maurice.

300
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:07,280
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

301
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:08,560
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

302
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:11,140
I was washing you, and all you did was a basket, and that's how you said the weight

303
00:18:11,140 --> 00:18:16,320
of... Ah! Well, that's the first French I've understood.

304
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:17,500
Wait, my nut sack!

305
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:18,760
My nut sack!

306
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:22,880
Ah! I never thought we'd do it.

307
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:24,700
No, I never doubted it for a second.

308
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:26,740
At least we've got to catch that metro to DeGaul Airport.

309
00:18:27,080 --> 00:18:28,920
Not DeGaul, Orly Airport.

310
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:29,980
Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

311
00:18:29,980 --> 00:18:30,740
I didn't screw this one up.

312
00:18:30,740 --> 00:18:31,580
I checked the ticket, see?

313
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:34,540
No, but my flight's leaving out of Orly, see?

314
00:18:40,940 --> 00:18:42,980
Well, then I guess this is goodbye.

315
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:45,780
I know this trip wasn't a pleasure for you.

316
00:18:45,780 --> 00:18:46,760
No, you go first.

317
00:18:47,220 --> 00:18:47,960
No, you go first.

318
00:18:49,380 --> 00:18:51,020
This is harder than I expected.

319
00:18:51,020 --> 00:18:53,740
All of a sudden, I can't say goodbye.

320
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:54,780
Well, then don't.

321
00:18:56,780 --> 00:18:57,800
Just say, we.

322
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:00,180
That means yes, Mike.

323
00:19:00,360 --> 00:19:03,540
I know, but the only other word in French I know is aah!

324
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:05,440
I'm sure that didn't seem appropriate.

325
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:09,740
Here. This is my address in California.

326
00:19:10,660 --> 00:19:11,860
You can read, can't you?

327
00:19:12,540 --> 00:19:15,560
Yeah. Thank you.

328
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:17,600
Believe it or not, this was...

329
00:19:19,840 --> 00:19:20,960
This was... You having fun?

330
00:19:22,180 --> 00:19:27,040
Yeah. It wasn't too horrible to be with, was I?

331
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:30,220
I mean, I can be so rigid, but I am working on it.

332
00:19:30,260 --> 00:19:31,240
Keep working on it.

333
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:45,980
Well, I guess we gotta go.

334
00:19:48,500 --> 00:19:49,820
I'm going to miss you, Mike.

335
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:52,660
And for what it's worth,

336
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:55,800
you're not the screw up that you think you are.

337
00:19:56,860 --> 00:19:59,960
And I mean that pretty much the way it sounds.

338
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:29,520
What's this picture?

339
00:20:29,520 --> 00:20:32,380
That's the alley where that crazy Spanish guy was chasing me.

340
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:35,460
That is the men's room where I ducked in on the run.

341
00:20:36,380 --> 00:20:37,000
Nice year, little.

342
00:20:37,120 --> 00:20:39,600
Thank you. Hey, what's this?

343
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:42,140
Oh, those are my mug shots.

344
00:20:42,840 --> 00:20:44,500
You know, they usually don't let you keep those things.

345
00:20:44,900 --> 00:20:46,200
Nice lighting. Thank you.

346
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:47,880
Hey, who's the babe?

347
00:20:48,180 --> 00:20:49,260
That is Amy Boudelay.

348
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:50,240
That's the girl that I met.

349
00:20:50,700 --> 00:20:54,200
Eh, at first she was kind of a drag, but then later on she turned out to be...

350
00:20:55,580 --> 00:20:56,160
kind of a drag.

351
00:20:57,320 --> 00:20:58,920
This doesn't look like a very fun trip.

352
00:20:59,540 --> 00:21:01,920
Look, Ben, you do not go to Europe just to have fun.

353
00:21:02,180 --> 00:21:05,000
You go there to experience an older, richer culture.

354
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:06,520
Any more urinals?

355
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:09,960
Hey, that must be Mom and Dad.

356
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:13,140
Uh, well, listen, Ben, I really don't think I'm ready to hear about the trip yet,

357
00:21:13,140 --> 00:21:15,680
okay? They'll probably blame me for selling them the lousy tour.

358
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:17,360
All right, if they ask, I'm not home.

359
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:19,360
Go on. I can handle Mom and Dad.

360
00:21:19,460 --> 00:21:21,140
Trust me. Okay, thanks.

361
00:21:22,300 --> 00:21:24,540
Hey, Ben! How are you?

362
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:26,280
So, you guys are home.

363
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:27,940
Yeah. How was your trip?

364
00:21:27,940 --> 00:21:29,800
I hope your pictures are better than Mike's.

365
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:33,600
Mike's home? Uh, Mike who?

366
00:21:35,780 --> 00:21:39,020
Why are we wasting our time talking about somebody who's not even here?

367
00:21:39,420 --> 00:21:40,820
Let's see those darn pictures.

368
00:21:41,420 --> 00:21:45,460
Sorry, Ben, no pictures, but I do have plenty of postcards.

369
00:21:46,620 --> 00:21:48,400
Man, you guys saw a lot of neat stuff.

370
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:49,920
Not any of it.

371
00:21:51,640 --> 00:21:55,440
Mommy! Mommy! Thank God you're back.

372
00:21:55,700 --> 00:21:57,920
I wrote a check for the thingy I broke most of the time.

373
00:21:57,940 --> 00:21:59,240
Your children are here, I think.

374
00:21:59,420 --> 00:22:02,560
The only good thing about this week is Ed left two days ago.

375
00:22:02,740 --> 00:22:04,740
Oh, don't worry, I'll take a cab.

376
00:22:04,940 --> 00:22:06,020
See you, bye.

377
00:22:09,460 --> 00:22:11,620
I think Grandma's had a tough week.

378
00:22:15,700 --> 00:22:18,260
Hello? It's worse than I thought, Ben.

379
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:20,700
Mom and Dad have completely disappeared.

380
00:22:21,260 --> 00:22:24,420
At this rate, it looks like I may have to stay here a couple of weeks.

381
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:26,980
Dad, I think you better handle this one.

382
00:22:27,940 --> 00:22:51,080
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

383
00:22:51,080 --> 00:22:51,220
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

384
00:22:51,220 --> 00:22:53,260
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

385
00:22:55,740 --> 00:23:00,040
I'm sorry. Now, these things happen all the time, you know?

386
00:23:00,040 --> 00:23:03,240
A couple's sailing along in a marriage and all of a sudden, poofed.

387
00:23:03,580 --> 00:23:04,860
What poofed? This poofed.

388
00:23:04,900 --> 00:23:05,960
Who poofed? You poofed.

389
00:23:05,980 --> 00:23:06,640
I didn't poof.

390
00:23:06,660 --> 00:23:37,020
Poof. I'm sorry.
